Subject: [PATCH] gui: a WebView2 that never starts asks before magpie ends
 (#5773, BHXGGGGG)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On Windows, Wails waits 60s for the WebView2 controller and, on a
timeout, reports through ErrorHandler and exits the whole process — the
reporter's log shows magpie 0.1.3226 ending with its gateway after
"timed out after 1m0s waiting for the WebView2 controller", the fourth
such exit in the log in five days. The desktop build has no console for
the reason to land in, so from Explorer the exit is silent, the way a
magpie with no runtime came up to nothing (#1806, ufec).

Wails' errorCallback takes no override: it runs the ErrorHandler magpie
sets and then os.Exit(1) itself, skipping OnShutdown. Two things now
happen before that exit, on Windows and for the initialisation failures
that exit follows (the controller wait timing out, the loader not
answering, the runtime version untold, the browser path gone, the
controller not made — the strings errorCallback hands over; errors
reported without exiting, a shortcut that didn't register or an event
handler's panic, keep getting only the log):

- A box of Windows' own asks whether to start magpie again, in the
  app's languages (the webView2Notice way of #1806). The box can't be
  shown from ErrorHandler itself — it runs on the thread Wails makes
  its windows on, and ufec measured one hanging 122s there — so it goes
  up on a thread of its own and ErrorHandler waits, a bounded 5 minutes:
  a box nobody answers must not hang a half-started magpie. Yes starts
  magpie again beside this one (RelaunchBinary; the new process waits
  for this one to exit before it takes the gateway's port,
  AwaitPredecessor).
- The tidying OnShutdown would have done runs either way (one closure
  now shared by both): that exit is os.Exit, and the failover Codex was
  left pointing at this process would retry a gateway that is gone, the
  harm OnShutdown's own comment records (Leon920717).

Elsewhere ErrorHandler keeps logging only: Wails exits over webview
errors on Windows alone, and runtime ones (a Navigate that failed, a
script that didn't run) keep doing so — a box naming WebView2 would say
the wrong reason; those leave with the log.

Run (darwin):
- go test -race -count=1 -run 'TestWebView2Fatal|TestWebView2ExitNotice|
  TestWebview2ExitAskRestartTidyUp|TestWebView2Missing|TestWebView2Notice|
  TestWebView2ArgsMergeTheUsers' ./internal/gui: ok.
- TestDataFolderMoveRestarts, TestGatewayFixQuitsOnlyAMagpie: ok.
- gofmt -l clean; GOOS=windows go build ./internal/gui, also -tags nogui,
  and go vet: ok.
- Ablation: the orchestration hunk out of runWebview2Exit →
  TestWebview2ExitAskRestartTidyUp red ("ran [], want [restart
  shutdown]") → restored → green.
- Not tried on real Windows (none here): the box, the restart and the
  tidying on a live exit. The reporter's log is the live shape; the
  tests pin the dispatch and the orchestration around it.

Fixes #5773

